{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/83041-wraith20-can-we-fix-the-whole-all-specters-are-buddies-thing","id":83041,"title":"Wraith20: Can we fix the whole all specters are buddies thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-03T01:47:43-08:00","id":83041,"title":"Wraith20: Can we fix the whole all specters are buddies thing?","content":"Okay so the biggest issue I had about wraith was all Spectres were on the same side... They would even try to lure you into giving in to oblivion for things like revenge, but that doesn't make a lot of sense in many cases because many of the people Wraiths would want to have revenge on would be specters. One of the things I liked about Po souls in Exalted is they weren't necessarily Buddies, they were just naturally pack oriented. But I have issues with it in Wraith. I get there is that whole Hivemind thing, but this needs to be touched upon so it feels less forced. Seriously why on Earth would the Damned get along? I mean in the Labyrinth they start developing tenancies towards soul cannibalism when they start evolving into Hekatonhires. <br /> <br /> I would like it if this was touched upon so the damned situation seems more natural, rather then all insane douchers get along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:26:55-08:00","id":83135,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>Doomslayers</i> has some great fiction involving Coldheart threatened/bribing a Onceborn. It also has a neat take on the Hive-mind; it was something that was present (Coldheart could feel it), but wasn't compelled by it. I also got the impression that his Companions were a bit more cognizant than the &quot;typical&quot; Shadow-eaten. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T07:35:51-08:00","id":83156,"title":"","content":"You may want to dig into Orpheus; the later books essentially revolve around a Spectre civil war. This could just as easily be extrapolated to in-fighting between Malfeans (fought largely by their servants, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T07:46:39-08:00","id":83164,"title":"","content":"Yeah as Naz said there is material out there that points out the Spectres aren't as unified as they appear. Of course you have to keep in mind few wraiths, if any, actually know this. Though that does get a bit more fleshed out in Orpheus with things like the Orphan-Grinders, Spectres that actually began to recover bits of who they were and eventually broke free of the hivemind and turned back into a spirit, and the Spectre Civil War between the forces of Grandma and those Malfeans opposed to 'her'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T09:54:39-08:00","id":83270,"title":"","content":"The book <i>Spectres</i> also talks about how things aren't all rosy between various spectre classes. It's not exactly all it could/should be, but it's not a bad resource for how spectres aren't the Borg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:24:11-08:00","id":83465,"title":"","content":"As I think every one pointed out, <i>Spectres</i> is the book you're really looking for. There's just as much back-biting, cliquishness, elitism, and outright treachery on Oblivion's side as there is anywhere else. They're just <i>better</i> at putting on a unified front, or the appearance of one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T15:12:15-08:00","id":83510,"title":"","content":"All that having been said, I wouldn't mind it being made more obvious in the core book - it's easy to make the mistake that spectres are a bit borgish if you don't have some of the supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T07:34:40-08:00","id":86747,"title":"","content":"Dark Reflections touches on spectre society, they dont all get along, not by a long shot. Its a great book that you should look into for your answers, and also has some great art and ideas for game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:01:05-08:00","id":86870,"title":"","content":"Anyone who's ever worked for a large company or organization can tell you that you may all work for the same boss, but that doesn't mean everyone's rowing in the same direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}